From 1bab048474b8b0508f34a8fe4ca7d99538e30429 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Somalapuram Amaranath <somalapuram@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 08:30:46 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] camera: compile in the verbose logging that names the buffer
 layout

BRING-UP ONLY -- revert before shipping.

The external camera preview is monochrome while a still capture taken from
the same decoded frame comes out in colour. That split is the whole clue,
and it follows the two code paths exactly: the JPEG is encoded from
mYu12Frame by libjpeg on the CPU, whereas the preview is written into a
gralloc buffer whose layout comes from lockYCbCr() and is then classified by
getFourCcFromLayout() -- purely from the distance between the cb and cr
pointers and the chroma_step.

formatConvert() reports no error on any frame, so both sides believe they
agree about that layout while the chroma never reaches the consumer. That is
the signature of the allocator and the HAL disagreeing silently, not of a
conversion failure, and it is a live suspect on this device because the
gralloc implementation here is a patched minigbm.

The values that would settle it -- the y/cb/cr pointers, the strides, the
chroma_step, and the fourcc derived from them -- are already logged in
ExternalCameraDeviceSession.cpp, but at ALOGV, which LOG_NDEBUG=1 compiles
out of release builds. Setting log.tag.ExtCamDev=V does not bring them back:
the statements are not in the binary. That was tried first and cost a boot.

This logs per frame at 30fps, which is why it is temporary.

Change-Id: Icf9d875d4ac2d0a13bb18fa05413c46815c48950
---
 camera/device/default/Android.bp | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/camera/device/default/Android.bp b/camera/device/default/Android.bp
index 10cee12cd1..af4dd111e6 100644
--- a/camera/device/default/Android.bp
+++ b/camera/device/default/Android.bp
@@ -31,6 +31,25 @@ cc_library_shared {
         "hidl_defaults",
     ],
     proprietary: true,
+
+    // BRING-UP ONLY -- revert before shipping.
+    //
+    // The preview is monochrome while a still capture from the same frame is
+    // in colour. That split is the whole clue: the JPEG is encoded from
+    // mYu12Frame by libjpeg on the CPU, whereas the preview is written into a
+    // gralloc buffer whose layout comes from lockYCbCr and is then classified
+    // by getFourCcFromLayout(). formatConvert() reports no error, so both
+    // sides believe they agree, yet the chroma is not reaching the consumer.
+    //
+    // The values that would settle it are logged -- the cb/cr pointers,
+    // strides and chroma_step in ExternalCameraDeviceSession.cpp, and the
+    // fourcc getFourCcFromLayout() derives from them -- but only at ALOGV,
+    // which LOG_NDEBUG=1 compiles out of release builds. Setting
+    // log.tag.ExtCamDev=V cannot bring them back; that was already tried and
+    // cost a boot. The statements have to be compiled in.
+    //
+    // This is verbose (per frame at 30fps), which is why it is temporary.
+    cflags: ["-DLOG_NDEBUG=0"],
     srcs: [
         "ExternalCameraDevice.cpp",
         "ExternalCameraDeviceSession.cpp",
